    "title": "Gaffney will not appeal move to 4A - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Pete Yanity No media credit provided. ,\n2 hours ago\nGaffney will not appeal its move from 5A down to 4A in the South Carolina High School League’s new reclassification plan, the school’s principal announced Wednesday.\nIt means they’ll no longer be in the same class with local rivals Spartanburg, Dorman, Byrnes, and Boiling Springs.\n“For the best interest of all athletic programs at Gaffney High, because moving back to 5A affects all sports, we will not appeal to return back to 5A for the next realignment cycle,” Gaffney principal Dr. Eric Blanton said Wednesday.\nHe indicates the school’s coaches still have the autonomy to schedule and play whichever programs they choose and presumably Indians teams will continue to do that with neighboring school, just not as region rivals.\nThe SCHSL recently revealed its two-year reclassification plan and schools had until 1pm Wednesday to file an appeal.\nAccording to The State newspaper, only two area schools will file with Eastside asking to move from 5A down to 4A and Greer Middle College desiring a move from 3A to 2A.\nAppeals hearings will be held next Tuesday and Wednesday.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WSPA 7NEWS.",
